<title>UK: UK monthly monetary meeting to start at 1100 GMT.</title>
<headline>UK monthly monetary meeting to start at 1100 GMT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The UK monthly monetary meeting between Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke and Bank of England Governor Eddie George is still due to start at 1100 GMT this morning, a Treasury spokesman said.</p>
<p>A Reuter poll of 20 economist showed that all believed UK interest rates would be left unchanged at six percent after the meeting.</p>
<p>-- Cheryl Juckes, London newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
